# Sources for searched replies: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# (info and bestmove), fisher-2aj rules 1, 7 and 10, and python-chess 1.11.2
# for the independently checked exact values. Written 2026-11-23.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/,
# the owner decision of 2026-11-23 that a FEN in which the color that is not
# the side to move is in check is rejected, and shakmaty 0.30.3, which rejects
# the second FEN below as an illegal position (OPPOSITE_CHECK).
# Written 2026-11-23. The expected values were chosen by the owner.
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# White to move while the black king on e8 is attacked by the rook on e1.
> position fen 4k3/8/8/8/8/8/8/4RK2 w - - 0 1
# Owner decision of 2026-11-23: one diagnostic naming the check.
< info string {message:in check}
> isready
# UCI isready/readyok.
< readyok
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8g8, then h6g7 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 21, 30 and 730 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 nodes 782
# Owner-approved example: the original position still has its sole legal move.
< bestmove h8g8
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
